{"format":"edusim-world","version":1,"exportedAt":"2026-08-17T00:29:20.346Z","records":[{"id":"d24af31d-2883-4ae5-ac5e-a16be71fe47d","kind":"world-theme","theme":"redsquare","createdAt":1786926560283,"transform":{"position":[0,0,0],"rotation":[0,0,0],"scale":[1,1,1]}},{"id":"833af000-97db-4186-90d3-3bf13e35aa4a","createdAt":1786926560284,"transform":{"position":[0,2.220446049250313e-14,-100],"rotation":[0,0,0],"scale":[1,1,1]},"kind":"preset-prop","prop":"st-basils","options":{"height":155,"radius":44,"seed":5}},{"id":"2e81cd58-a031-4caa-b094-276d85c7b319","createdAt":1786926560285,"transform":{"position":[-40,1.021405182655144e-14,-46],"rotation":[0,0.4353532751523024,0],"scale":[1,1,1]},"kind":"preset-prop","prop":"info-placard","options":{"eyebrow":"Nine churches on one foundation","title":"St Basil's Cathedral","accent":"#c8452f","body":"Eight chapels arranged as an eight-pointed star around a ninth in the middle, each with its own dome — and no two domes are alike. Ivan the Terrible had it built in 1561 to mark a victory. The story that he blinded the architect so it could never be repeated is almost certainly untrue: the same man went on to build something else."}},{"id":"0deb7167-6244-43bc-80c8-f18549144673","createdAt":1786926560286,"transform":{"position":[40,1.021405182655144e-14,-46],"rotation":[0,-0.4353532751523024,0],"scale":[1,1,1]},"kind":"preset-prop","prop":"info-placard","options":{"eyebrow":"It was white for a hundred years","title":"The domes","accent":"#2e5fa8","body":"The colour is not original. The cathedral stood white with gold domes until the 1680s, and the spirals, chevrons and facets were painted on later. Nobody is certain why. The shape is not borrowed either — the tall tent roof in the middle is Russian, and you will not find it on a Byzantine church."}},{"id":"deea3cd8-4a7c-498f-a123-7cc2395b61f8","createdAt":1786926560287,"transform":{"position":[-74,7.549516567451064e-15,-34],"rotation":[0,1.5707963267948966,0],"scale":[1,1,1]},"kind":"preset-prop","prop":"kremlin-wall","options":{"length":86,"height":26,"depth":12,"seed":7}},{"id":"4cc0afea-e5bf-46f3-90ba-599c7f423b48","createdAt":1786926560288,"transform":{"position":[-74,4.893753096091302e-7,66],"rotation":[0,1.5707963267948966,0],"scale":[1,1,1]},"kind":"preset-prop","prop":"kremlin-wall","options":{"length":78,"height":26,"depth":12,"seed":9}},{"id":"c585d698-8f01-487b-a262-77d81d191fcc","createdAt":1786926560289,"transform":{"position":[-74,0,0],"rotation":[0,1.5707963267948966,0],"scale":[1,1,1]},"kind":"preset-prop","prop":"kremlin-tower","options":{"height":130,"base":18,"clock":true,"star":true,"seed":11}},{"id":"b270141e-7a78-4927-ba5e-8a7bb1aa5dbd","createdAt":1786926560290,"transform":{"position":[-74,0.02772791386787432,112],"rotation":[0,1.5707963267948966,0],"scale":[1,1,1]},"kind":"preset-prop","prop":"kremlin-tower","options":{"height":104,"base":15,"clock":false,"star":true,"seed":13}},{"id":"48f7e3dc-a113-4daa-823a-f3967176dfaa","createdAt":1786926560291,"transform":{"position":[-74,0.013522401752067204,-84],"rotation":[0,1.5707963267948966,0],"scale":[1,1,1]},"kind":"preset-prop","prop":"kremlin-tower","options":{"height":88,"base":13,"clock":false,"star":false,"seed":17}},{"id":"a9fd1c56-0f65-4116-aba5-f63617662e40","createdAt":1786926560292,"transform":{"position":[-52,-1.3322676295501878e-15,6],"rotation":[0,1.5707963267948966,0],"scale":[1,1,1]},"kind":"preset-prop","prop":"lenin-mausoleum","options":{"width":40,"height":24,"depth":30,"seed":13}},{"id":"dfd64c4b-16ca-4ca9-9e18-d0e3a2d785d3","createdAt":1786926560293,"transform":{"position":[-34,-7.549516567451064e-15,34],"rotation":[0,0.3764903344465229,0],"scale":[1,1,1]},"kind":"preset-prop","prop":"info-placard","options":{"eyebrow":"The clock is 20 feet across","title":"The Spasskaya Tower","accent":"#a8503c","body":"The gate tower on the square, and the one the chimes come from at New Year. The ruby star on top went up in 1937, replacing a double-headed imperial eagle. It is real glass, lit from inside, and it turns in the wind. The white upper stage is 200 years younger than the brick underneath it, which is why the two do not match."}},{"id":"aa9f4b83-a729-4851-bf91-aa15ccef969f","createdAt":1786926560294,"transform":{"position":[-30,3.552713678800501e-15,-16],"rotation":[0,0.21711131473490516,0],"scale":[1,1,1]},"kind":"preset-prop","prop":"info-placard","options":{"eyebrow":"Red and black granite","title":"Lenin's Mausoleum","accent":"#7a3630","body":"A stepped pyramid, deliberately low, so the leaders standing on the roof to watch a parade were level with the crowd rather than above it. The dark bands are labradorite, which is nearly black and flashes blue when the light catches it. Lenin himself had asked to be buried beside his mother."}},{"id":"f9a9ae31-3eb6-4bcb-8ce7-b31c7d6bd949","createdAt":1786926560295,"transform":{"position":[80,-3.552713678800501e-15,16],"rotation":[0,-1.5707963267948966,0],"scale":[1,1,1]},"kind":"preset-prop","prop":"gum-store","options":{"length":190,"height":46,"depth":34,"seed":17}},{"id":"49e7e61c-582d-49e5-bfda-aac3bc2af378","createdAt":1786926560296,"transform":{"position":[40,-1.021405182655144e-14,46],"rotation":[0,-0.49555167348582857,0],"scale":[1,1,1]},"kind":"preset-prop","prop":"info-placard","options":{"eyebrow":"A shopping arcade under glass","title":"GUM","accent":"#8c3f2c","body":"Built in 1893 with an iron and glass roof over three parallel arcades — the same engineering as a railway station, put to shopping. Under the Soviet Union it was the state department store, and for a long stretch it was mostly queues. The fountain in the middle is where Muscovites still arrange to meet."}},{"id":"95101416-f9cd-4043-85c0-4a51d9ed4e40","createdAt":1786926560297,"transform":{"position":[0,0.21156888369356075,152],"rotation":[0,3.141592653589793,0],"scale":[1,1,1]},"kind":"preset-prop","prop":"history-museum","options":{"length":120,"height":62,"depth":40,"seed":19}},{"id":"c71be5c6-6